            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "I don’t have live news access, so I can’t verify the very latest Perseverance rover update in real time. My knowledge is current only through **June 2024**.\n\nAs of then, NASA’s **Mars Perseverance rover** was continuing its mission in **Jezero Crater**, studying ancient river-delta deposits and collecting rock core samples that could help determine whether microbial life ever existed on Mars. Key ongoing themes included:\n\n- **Sample collection:** Perseverance had cached multiple scientifically valuable rock and regolith samples for possible future return to Earth.\n- **Search for ancient habitability:** The rover was examining sedimentary rocks formed in watery environments billions of years ago.\n- **Jezero Crater exploration:** It had moved from the crater floor into delta and margin regions, which are considered especially promising for preserving biosignatures.\n- **Ingenuity helicopter:** NASA’s Ingenuity Mars Helicopter ended its mission in early 2024 after rotor damage, after far exceeding expectations with dozens of flights.\n- **Mars Sample Return uncertainty:** NASA was reassessing the Mars Sample Return architecture due to cost and schedule concerns.\n\nFor the most current news, the best source is NASA’s Perseverance mission page or NASA/JPL’s Mars rover updates.",
